\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\iff\alpha2\sqrt{\varphi(x_{1}+y_{1})}=(1-\alpha-\beta)2\sqrt{\varphi(y_{1}-x_{1})}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\iff\alpha^{2}(x_{1}+y_{1})=(1-\alpha-\beta)^{2}(y_{1}-x_{1})$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\iff x_{1}^{*}=y_{1}\frac{(1-\alpha-\beta)^{2}-\alpha^{2}}{(1-\alpha-\beta)^{2}+\alpha^{2}}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since 
\begin_inset Formula $M1$
\end_inset

 is an expected utility maximizer, then 
\begin_inset Formula $F\succsim G\iff E_{F}u_{1}\geq E_{G}u_{1}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Note, we know that if 
\begin_inset Formula $M1$
\end_inset

 invests all of 
\begin_inset Formula $y_{1}$
\end_inset

 in the safe asset, then 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{G}u_{1}=\sqrt{\varphi y_{1}}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thus, the manager's optimal investment strategy is given by:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $x_{1}=\begin{cases}
x_{1}^{*} & \mbox{if}\ E_{F}u_{1}>\sqrt{\varphi y_{1}}\\
0 & \mbox{otherwise}
