\begin_layout Section*
Extra Assigned Problem
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Consider an expected utility maximizer with utility index 
\begin_inset Formula $u(x)=-e^{-ax}$
\end_inset

 with 
\begin_inset Formula $a>0$
\end_inset

 and initial wealth 
\begin_inset Formula $w>0$
\end_inset

.
 There is a risk free asset that has a return of 
\begin_inset Formula $2$
\end_inset

 (if the agent invest 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 dollars, then she receives 
\begin_inset Formula $2x$
\end_inset

).
 There is also a risky asset with random return 
\begin_inset Formula $1$
\end_inset

 with probability 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha>0$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $3$
\end_inset

 with probability 
\begin_inset Formula $(1-\alpha)$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
(a) Set up the portfolio choice problem for the agent (denote the amount
 invested in the risky asset by 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 and its optimal value by 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{*}$
\end_inset

).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We assume that the agent is an expected utility maximizer, and from his
 utility index, we know that he is risk averse
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $F$
\end_inset

 denote the c.d.f of the random return 
\begin_inset Formula $z$
\end_inset

 for the risky asset, and let 
\begin_inset Formula $G$
\end_inset

 denote the c.d.f of the certain return for the safe asset
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since the agen is an expected utility maximizer, then 
\begin_inset Formula $F\succsim G\iff E_{F}u\geq E_{G}u$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Note, if the agent invests all of his wealth in the safe asset, then 
\begin_inset Formula $E_{G}u=-e^{-a(2w)}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
So, the agent's optimal investment strategy is given by:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $x=\begin{cases}
x^{*} & \mbox{if}\ E_{F}u>-e^{-a(2w)}\\
\{0,x^{*}\} & \mbox{if}\ E_{F}u=-e^{-a(2w)}\\
0 & \mbox{if}\ E_{F}u<-e^{-a(2w)}
\end{cases}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For any realization of the random return 
\begin_inset Formula $z$
\end_inset

, the agent's portfolio 
\begin_inset Formula $(x,w-x)$
\end_inset

 pays 
\begin_inset Formula $xz+2(w-x)$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thus, the agent's choice problem for the amount invested in the risky asset
 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 is:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula ${\displaystyle \max_{0\le x\leq w}}\ \alpha\left[-e^{-a\left(2w-x\right)}\right]+(1-\alpha)\left[-e^{-a\left(2w+x\right)}\right]={\displaystyle \max_{0\le x\leq w}}\ -e^{-2aw}\left[\alpha(e^{ax})+(1-\alpha)(e^{-ax})\right]$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
(b) Under what conditions is 
\begin_inset Formula $x^{*}>0$
\end_inset

? Interpret.
\end_layout

